accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final type  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  operation date  01 removed_month 98 accessioned on  01 removed_month 98 at 13 49 clinical data  bilateral breast reduction                                                                                      final diagnosis     breast  right   reduction mammoplasty  invasive ductal carcinoma  removed_date cm  grade 2 of 3  negative for lymphatic or blood vascular invasion  see note below  ductal carcinoma in situ  associated with and extending a small distance away from the invasive tumor  fibrocystic changes  with moderate ductal epithelial hyperplasia  harboring microcalcifications  note  because the right reduction mammoplasty specimen is received as numerous fragments  margins cannot be assessed  the tumor is in two of the smallest fragments  with little surrounding normal tissue   and a largest tumor dimension is estimated from slides  both specimens are re examined grossly for other lesions  no areas suspicious for invasive tumor are identified in the right   the tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  the tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  see note  note  in this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  14 removed_month 98 at 16 08 gross description  received fresh   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and  l breast   is a 580 g reduction mammoplasty specimen  consisting of an irregular removed_date x removed_date x 2 4cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with an overlying triangular removed_date x 5 0cm portion of skin  a removed_date x removed_date x 2 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with an overlying triangular removed_date x 4 5cm portion of skin  and a removed_date x removed_date x 3 0cm aggregate of multiple pieces of fibroadipose tissue  within the smaller of the two fragments with attached skin  there is a removed_date x removed_date x 1 2cm ill defined  white  slightly firm lesion  which is entirely submitted in cassettes a h  additional representative sections of breast parenchyma are submitted in cassettes i j  received fresh   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and  r breast   is an 820 g reduction mammoplasty specimen  consisting of an irregular removed_date x removed_date x 3 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a triangular removed_date x 6 0cm portion of attached skin  a removed_date x removed_date x 2 0cm irregular fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a triangular removed_date x 5 0cm portion of attached skin  and a removed_date x removed_date x 3 0cm aggregate of multiple pieces of fibroadipose tissue  there are several areas of slightly firm  irregular  white tan parenchyma  of which representative sections are submitted in k t  re examination of the specimens after microscopical examination reveals that two small fragments from the right mastectomy specimen  removed_date x removed_date x 1 0cm and removed_date x removed_date x 0 6cm  are harder and whiter than the other fragments  these are entirely submitted  the former in u v  and the latter in w  no similar lesions are found in the right   reduction mammoplasty   report_end  , Moderate_(grade_II).
