accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  finaltype  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  accessioned on  30 removed_month 93 at 13 59 clinical data  right breast carcinoma rule out right   biopsy  infiltrating ductal carcinoma  grade 2  invading lymphatics and extending close to a margin of the specimen  intraductal carcinoma  see note  note  invasion of blood vessels is not seen  diagnosis by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  03 removed_month 93 at 09 03                                                                                     receptor immunohistochemistry addendum     results of staining of fixed tissue for hormone receptor proteins breast  right   the tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  the tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  see note  note  in this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical p